course: dictionary
lesson: 10586
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words wear different coats. Underground can be an adjective, an adverb or a noun, and its meaning changes with the sentence. «There is an underground passage from the river-bank right up into the middle of Toad Hall.» Here underground means below the surface of the ground, as in a tunnel dug under the earth.
explain: Context tells you which meaning to use. «The Mole feels lively underground, because he is a digger.» Mole is a digger, so the words digger and lively show that underground means below the ground, where he digs. Try your meaning in the sentence: does "below the ground" still make sense? Yes, so you have found it.
explain: When underground is a noun with the, as in «the underground», it means a railway that runs in tunnels under a city. In London it is called the Tube, and in the USA it is the subway. Context always gives you the clue: the words train, station or tunnel tell you that this is the railway, not the soil.
fact: Underground means below the surface of the ground.
fact: The underground is a railway that runs in tunnels under a city.
fact: Underground can also mean secret or hidden from the authorities, such as an underground group.
fact: Phrases to know: underground station, underground train, underground water, go underground.
fact: Regional words: in London the underground railway is called the Tube; in the USA it is the subway.
exercise: «Badger's great secret: there is an underground passage from the river-bank right up into the middle of Toad Hall.» What does underground mean here? | Up high in the trees | Covered in snow | *Below the ground, in a tunnel | Floating on the water
exercise: Priya catches the underground to school in London. What is the underground? | A shop on the high street | A type of cave in the hills | A bus that drives on the road | *A railway that runs in tunnels under the city
exercise: «The fennec fox's ears also hear prey moving underground.» What does prey moving underground suggest? | Birds flying above the trees | Water rising in a river | *Small animals moving below the ground | Stones falling from a hill
test: «Coal and oil are found underground.» What does underground mean in this sentence? | Up in the sky | *Below the surface of the ground | On the roof of a house | Under the sea, far from land
test: Which use of underground means secret or hidden? | Worms live underground in the soil | *An underground group met in a cellar, hiding from the soldiers | A train ran underground to the station | Rabbits dig underground burrows
exam: In «The termites live in the nest underground», what does underground mean? | Above the mound | Inside a big tree | Very cold | *Below the ground
